+# Software Factory pages
+
+This folder adds the Software Factory's pages to Agent Canvas for spec-driven, governed delivery:
+
+| Page | Route | Reads |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Autopilot (Home) | `/autopilot` | Goal box, autonomy dial, budget, setup status, the list of runs |
+| Pipeline | `/autopilot/runs/:runId/:workOrderKey?` | One run: stage lanes, waves of work orders, decisions, each work order's agents and checks |
+| Inbox | `/inbox` | Decisions Autopilot leaves to a person, across runs; the sidebar shows how many wait |
+| Requirements | `/requirements/:changeId?` | OpenSpec changes: proposal, specs with scenarios, design, tasks |
+| Work orders | `/work-orders/:workOrderId?` | Backlog.md tasks, as a board with a detail panel |
+| Audit log | `/audit-log` | The factory's hash-chained audit log |
+
+The data comes from the Software Factory API (`apps/server` in the software-factory
+repo), not from the OpenHands agent server. Vite proxies `/sf-api` to it
+(`SF_API_URL`, default `http://127.0.0.1:4317`). Autopilot's agents are ordinary
+OpenHands conversations started by the API, so every one of them opens in Canvas
+("Open in Canvas" on the Pipeline). Hand-started work orders still use "Start with an
+agent", which calls `useCreateConversation` with the workspace as the working folder
+and a brief written by the API.
+
+## Files
+
+```
+api.ts                 Typed client for /sf-api (shapes match apps/server/src/autopilot/routes.ts)
+hooks.ts               React Query hooks, and live updates over one shared Server-Sent Events stream
+copy.ts                The pages' words (English and Spanish)
+factory-nav-links.tsx  Sidebar entries, with the Inbox badge
+factory-routes.ts      The factory's routes, spread into src/routes.ts
+routes/                The pages
+components/            Page frame, markdown, badges, the decision card, and the plan/approve/start-agent dialogs
+```
+
+## Outside this folder
+
+Only three upstream files are touched, so pulling new OpenHands releases stays easy:
+
+- `src/routes.ts`: `...factoryRoutes` and its import (new pages go in `factory-routes.ts`)
+- `src/components/features/sidebar/sidebar-rail-body.tsx`: `<FactoryNavLinks />`
+- `vite.config.ts`: the `/sf-api` proxy
+
+## Rules the pages follow
+
+- Moving a work order to the last status is an approval. Only the Approve dialog
+  does it, and it records who approved and their note.
+- If a work order reaches the last status any other way (an agent ran the
+  Backlog.md CLI, someone edited the file), the API flags it as not approved and
+  the board shows it.
+- Autopilot decisions happen only through an Inbox item's buttons (or Pause, Resume
+  and Cancel on the Pipeline). The API records who chose what; a choice that needs a
+  note can't be sent without one, and cancelling asks to confirm.
+- Strings live in `copy.ts`, not `src/i18n/translation.json`, to keep the
+  factory self-contained. Other Canvas languages fall back to English.
+
+## Working on these pages without model logins
+
+Run the scripted fake agent server and point the API at it:
+
+```
+pnpm --filter @sf/server fake-agents                         # 127.0.0.1:18100
+SF_AGENT_SERVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:18100 pnpm dev:api
+```
+
+Its agents write a valid OpenSpec change, build three work orders (one fails its test
+once, one touches `src/auth/` so its merge waits for you) and pass review.
